# ======================== GRPC ========================

How does netflix handles communication between 1000 of microservices ?
If your answer is REST, then it is wrong, although rest is simple send a json request and receives a json response
but to do so, you need to serialize and desearilize, if you are doing billions of these calls then its a problem 
then it starts adding up, there are lot of microservices which are interlinked, if one of the api response is changed little bit then it can starts a chain reaction 

The fix was bringing GRPC instead of rest 

What is GRPC
Uses protocol buffers (binary serialization) Sends data directly in binary 
Runs of HTTP/2 (Single connection)
Services share a .proto schema (contract). Client/server code is generated from it. Breaking schema changes are detected during code generation or compilation instead of causing runtime failures.
